{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Itinerary for a Journey to the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\n**Act I Scene I: The Arrival in Nippon’s Fair Capital**\n\nUpon the morrow’s morn dost thou alight in Tokyo’s bustling gate where neon lights do dance like fairies in the night. Seek first the ancient temple of Senso-ji in Asakusa where incense doth weave its sacred sighs. Pray to the gods and partake of rice cakes sweet as Cupid’s breath.\n\nFrom thence repair to the Imperial Palace where emperors of old did tread. Walk the gardens fair and ponder the fleeting nature of power as cherry blossoms drift upon the wind.\n\n**Act I Scene II: The Gardens and the Theatres**\n\nTo Ueno’s park repair where art and nature in sweet concord meet. The museums stand like nobles in their halls and the ponds reflect the heavens’ own gaze.\n\nIn the evening don thy finest robes and attend a play at the National Theatre. Witness the grace of Noh or the mirth of Kabuki where actors don faces bright as moonlit clouds.\n\n**Act II Scene I: The Road to Nikko’s Sacred Glades**\n\nUpon the third day take carriage to Nikko where mountains kiss the sky and temples rise like castles in the air. The Toshogu Shrine doth gleam with gold and craftsmanship beyond mortal ken. Walk the cedar-lined paths and heed the whispers of the forest’s heart.\n\n**Act II Scene II: The Lakes and the Legends**\n\nTo Hakone’s steaming waters do thou journey where hot springs cleanse the soul and Mount Fuji stands sentinel in silent majesty. Ride the pirate ship upon Lake Ashi and gaze upon the peak that poets sing.\n\nDost thou then bathe in waters hot and sulphurous as Vulcan’s own forge and let thy cares dissolve like mist before the sun.\n\n**Act III Scene I: The Ancient Capital of Nara**\n\nUpon the fifth morn set forth to Nara where deer do bow as courtiers of old. The Todai-ji’s great Buddha sits in quiet grandeur and the Kasuga Shrine’s lanterns glow like stars entangled in the boughs.\n\n**Act III Scene II: The Imperial City of Kyoto**\n\nTo Kyoto’s embrace do thou return where samurai once drew their swords and poets penned verses sweet as honey. The Kinkaku-ji doth gleam like a jewel set in a lotus pond and the Arashiyama’s bamboo grove doth whisper secrets to the winds.\n\nIn Gion’s lanes seek the geisha’s fleeting glance and if fortune doth smile upon thee partake of a tea ceremony where silence speaks louder than tongues.\n\n**Act IV Scene I: The Culmination in Osaka’s Bounty**\n\nTo Osaka’s fair city do thou journey where laughter rings like silver bells and the takoyaki doth sizzle hot in thy hand. The Dotonbori’s lights do blaze like a thousand suns and the castle’s walls stand proud as any king’s.\n\n**Act IV Scene II: The Farewell in Hiroshima’s Peace**\n\nUpon the final days visit Hiroshima where cranes of paper fold in memory of sorrow turned to hope. The Peace Memorial Park doth stand as a testament to man’s folly and his redemption.\n\nFrom thence take ship upon the Inland Sea and let thy heart be light as thou watchest the sunset paint the waters in hues of fire.\n\n**Epilogue: The Return**\n\nWhen the time cometh to depart from this enchanted land bear with thee the memories of sake shared with strangers and the kindness of those who spake not thy tongue yet understood thy heart.\n\nGo forth with the blessing of the gods and the promise that Japan’s beauty shall ever linger in thy soul like a sweet refrain. Fare thee well.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -1.2387763261795044}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.052233871072530746}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.27844080328941345}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.27144667506217957}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -1.6212332411669195e-05}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -2.3841830625315197e-06}, {"token": " It", "logprob": -0.38218143582344055}, {"token": "iner", "logprob": -0.0008715168805792928}, {"toke